# Hand-wrapped prose. Prettier reflows markdown, which would destroy deliberate line breaks in
# DESIGN.md, CLAUDE.md and the decision records. Likewise, `pnpm format` rewrites workflow docs.
*.md
.github/

# Generated output
web/dist/
web/.astro/
studio/dist/
studio/schema.json

# Written by `sanity dev`. studio/.gitignore already ignores it, but Prettier reads only the ROOT
# .gitignore, never a nested one — so a local `prettier --check .` failed on it while CI, which
# never has the directory, would not.
studio/.sanity/

# Claude Code worktrees: whole checkouts of this repo, nested inside it. Git ignores them through
# .git/info/exclude, which Prettier does not read — so without this, `pnpm format` in the main
# checkout would rewrite files in a worktree someone else is in the middle of editing.
.claude/worktrees/

# Composer writes this file too, on `composer require`, by its own rules. Two writers of one file
# is the churn studio/sanity.cli.ts records for TypeGen, and Composer is the one that owns it.
web/server/composer.json

# Lockfiles
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
